{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('map.json'))\nb14=[b for b in m['behaviors'] if b['id']=='B14-ballot-monotonicity'][0]\nb14['important_branches'].append(\\\"the shipped deployment configuration designates a leader (leader: 0.0.0.1 in aws.conf, with leaderless: false) and gives protocol SwiftPaxos, which run-time flags override; under the epaxos protocol that designation reaches Replica.BeTheLeader, so one replica carries IsLeader = true while the other replicas do not (S31-master-startup, S33-aws-config)\\\")\njson.dump(m,open('map.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nsrcs=[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S33-aws-config\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"aws.conf\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":30,\\\"end_line\\\":40,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"}]\nfb={\\\"ref_ids\\\":[\\\"B14-ballot-monotonicity\\\",\\\"S33-aws-config\\\",\\\"S31-master-startup\\\",\\\"S5-broadcasters\\\",\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\"],\n \\\"answered\\\":\\\"The remaining question about the deployed variant is answered from the configuration: the shipped aws.conf designates a leader alias (leader: 0.0.0.1, the first listed replica) and sets leaderless: false, with protocol SwiftPaxos that command-line flags override per run. Because the master's designation calls Replica.BeTheLeader on the marked replica (master startup and promotion on leader failure), running this configuration under the epaxos protocol leaves exactly one replica with IsLeader = true and the others with false, so makeBallot's raising loop is active on that replica while it recovers instances.\\\",\n \\\"remaining\\\":[\\\"whether IsLeader = true changes the confirmed recovery finding: the reasoning is that it only raises the new ballot further, so the recovering replica's self entry still announces the new ballot as its VBallot and remote values at older vbals are still skipped, but no check has been run with the flag set and the C1 claim's confirmed scope records IsLeader false\\\",\n   \\\"whether a promoted replica's higher ballots affect the accept-round completion or the crash finding in ways the existing checks do not cover\\\"],\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Reading the configuration closes the variant question with a document source and shows that the launched deployment is not uniformly IsLeader false, which matters for how far the confirmed findings are read. The claim scopes are left untouched; the variant is recorded as a map branch plus a remaining question rather than as an extension of any confirmed result.\\\",\n \\\"understanding\\\":\\\"updated\\\",\\\"question_updates\\\":{}}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Records the deployed variant for the ballot/leader flag: aws.conf designates a leader alias and sets leaderless false, so under the epaxos protocol one replica carries IsLeader = true. Adds the configuration as a source and one branch to B14; no claim, binding, edge or identity changes, and the unverified interaction with the confirmed finding is left as an explicit remaining question.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":srcs,\\\"map_path\\\":\\\"map.json\\\",\n \\\"map_changes\\\":{\\\"B14-ballot-monotonicity\\\":{\\\"impact\\\":\\\"clarification\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"A branch records the shipped configuration's leader designation and its consequence for the deployment variant (one replica with IsLeader true under the epaxos protocol).\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S33-aws-config\\\",\\\"S31-master-startup\\\"],\\\"preserves\\\":\\\"The ballot arithmetic, the master call sites already recorded and the ownership statement are unchanged; the addition is the deployed variant.\\\"}},\n \\\"feedback\\\":fb}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-aws-variant.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-aws-variant.json 2>&1 | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
